    {"id": "v10-le-comptoir-des-tontons", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 10, "badge": "NATURAL WINE", "name": "Le Comptoir des Tontons", "short": "Le Comptoir des Tontons", "lat": 47.0205, "lng": 4.8426, "tags": [], "productTags": ["Contemporary", "Wine"], "why": "Pépita Del Rosario and Richard Grocat opened the Comptoir in 1996 as an épicerie and cave à manger, seeking out small farmers and winemakers who refuse chemical shortcuts, years before natural wine had a following in Beaune. During lockdown the shop side grew into a fuller épicerie and wine shop. The plates are built from what sits on the shelves and from seasonal, organic-leaning produce; reviewers keep returning to the take-away wine list.", "address": "22 Rue du Faubourg Madeleine, 21200 Beaune", "phone": "+33 3 80 24 19 64", "hours": "Year-round as far as found; no annual closure published. Open now (late Oct): likely, Tue-Sat. Nov-Dec: no closure found. Auction weekend: Fri 13 and Sat 14 Nov fall on its days; Sun 15 and Mon 16 Nov are its closing days; no source on booking out · Call ahead: Pages Jaunes lists Tue-Sat afternoon to evening, Le Fooding morning and evening hours; both say closed Sunday and Monday; TripAdvisor marks the restaurant listing 'closed'", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Comptoir+des+Tontons+Beaune", "price_range": "EUR 32-48 menu (seen May 2026)", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-25", "hook": "Pépita Del Rosario's natural-wine épicerie and bistrot on the Faubourg Madeleine, trading since 1996.", "verdict": "A Raisin visitor in mid-2026 praises the list and Pépita herself, so the house trades; whether the table service runs as it once did is less clear, since Raisin and Le Fooding now file it as a shop and TripAdvisor flags it closed. Treat it as a natural-wine cellar first, call to ask about a table, and expect conviction over polish: some reviewers find the service rough.", "signature": "Whatever the seasonal plate is, with a natural bottle chosen at the shelf", "caveat": "Closed Sunday and Monday per Pages Jaunes and Le Fooding; table service unconfirmed for 2026, call first", "person": "Pépita Del Rosario (owner)", "dishes": [{"name": "Seasonal plate from organic-leaning produce", "note": "The house line in its own words: seasonal produce, organic-oriented cooking", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Pork from the kitchen", "note": "Singled out by a TripAdvisor reviewer; ask if it is on", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Natural wine to take away", "note": "The take-away list is what reviewers praise most consistently", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Épicerie preserves from small producers", "note": "The shelves the kitchen also cooks from, per Le Fooding", "kind": "dish"}], "reservation": "Call ahead; few seats and the table service is not confirmed for 2026", "neighborhood": "Faubourg Madeleine", "signal_chip": {"label": "Since 1996", "full": "Natural-wine épicerie and cave à manger founded in 1996 by Pépita Del Rosario and Richard Grocat", "cosign": "Raisin (visitor comment, mid-2026); Jancis Robinson; Le Fooding"}, "category": "wine"},
    {"id": "v11-enstase", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 11, "badge": "NATURAL WINE BAR", "name": "Enstase", "short": "Enstase", "lat": 47.0234, "lng": 4.8407, "tags": [], "productTags": ["Wine", "Bacaro"], "why": "Enstase opened as a company in September 2021 and works as three things at once: a cellar of natural, organic and biodynamic bottles (some 900 references from small estates, by its own listing), a bar, and a kitchen. Raisin's 2023 feature describes a cooking station that opens two evenings a week for shared plates and street-food bao. Beyond the wine there are ciders, kefirs, kombuchas and juices, which makes it the one counter in town for a guest off alcohol.", "address": "5 Rue Vergnette de Lamotte, 21200 Beaune", "phone": "+33 9 71 31 10 17", "hours": "Year-round as far as found; no annual closure published. Open now (late Oct): probably, unconfirmed. Nov-Dec: unknown. Auction weekend: Fri 13 Nov is a kitchen night in every listing; Sun 15 and Mon 16 Nov conflict across listings; no source on booking · Call ahead: Raisin lists the shop Mon-Sat with restaurant service Thu-Sat evenings; another Raisin wording says tapas and bao Thu-Mon; one directory shows Thu-Fri to 21:30, closed Mon and Sun; Raisin's 2023 feature says kitchen Thu and Fri only", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Enstase+Beaune", "price_range": "EUR 6-15 glass (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Unknown; call ahead for kitchen nights", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-25", "hook": "Natural-wine shop and bar off Place Carnot; an open kitchen does bao and shared plates late in the week.", "verdict": "The most recent dated evidence is a set of Raisin visitor comments from October 2025; nothing dated 2026 turned up, and listings disagree on which evenings the kitchen runs. It is still the natural-wine counter of central Beaune on paper. Send nobody without a call or a look at its own channels the same week.", "signature": "Bao and small plates from the open kitchen, with a glass of natural wine", "caveat": "Kitchen only on some evenings (Thu-Fri in 2023, later listings say Thu-Sat or longer); no 2026 evidence: call first", "dishes": [{"name": "Bao", "note": "Street-food buns from the open kitchen, the dish every write-up mentions", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Shared small plates from local produce", "note": "Tapas-style plates on kitchen nights", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Natural wine by the glass or bottle", "note": "Some 900 references from small estates, per its company listing", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Cider, kefir and kombucha", "note": "The low- and no-alcohol shelf most wine bars do not have", "kind": "drink"}], "web": "https://enstase.fr", "neighborhood": "Place Carnot", "signal_chip": {"label": "900 wines", "full": "Natural, organic and biodynamic cellar of about 900 references from small estates, with a bao kitchen on some evenings", "cosign": "Raisin (feature 2023, visitor comments Oct 2025)"}, "category": "wine", "hot_this_month": "Bao and small plates on its kitchen evenings, late in the week; listings disagree on which nights, so call before you plan the Friday of the auction weekend round it."},
    {"id": "v15-march-des-halles-saturday", "cat": "berth", "tier": "berth_top", "priority": 3, "badge": "SATURDAY MARKET", "name": "Marché des Halles (Saturday)", "short": "Marché des Halles (Satur", "lat": 47.0213, "lng": 4.8392, "tags": [], "productTags": ["Market", "Produce", "Cheese"], "why": "On Saturday morning the stalls fill the covered halles on Place de la Halle and spill across Place Fleury: hill-village producers with Époisses and Cîteaux, slabs of jambon persillé, honey, flowers, and in autumn the first wild mushrooms. The same halles host the Hospices wine auction each November, so the market stands where Burgundy sells its most famous barrels. Wednesday brings a smaller food-only market to the same square.", "address": "Place de la Halle and Place Fleury, 21200 Beaune", "phone": "+33 3 80 24 57 46 (contact listed by JDS)", "hours": "Year-round weekly market; OT lists each Saturday 1 Aug-26 Dec 2026. Open now (Sat 31 Oct): yes. Nov-Dec: yes, through Sat 26 Dec; the shift rule for 25 and 31 Dec does not touch a Saturday in 2026. Auction weekend: Sat 14 Nov is inside the listed run but the halles host the auction on Sun 15 Nov; whether the market is displaced is not published · Saturday 08:00-12:00 (Office de Tourisme de Beaune, JDS); some listings say to about 13:00. Wednesday morning smaller 'marché gourmand', listed through 30 Dec 2026", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marché+des+Halles+(Saturday)+Beaune", "price_range": "Market prices; free entry", "reservation": "Walk-in", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-25", "hook": "Beaune's Saturday morning market, under the covered halles and out across Place Fleury.", "verdict": "The Office de Tourisme lists it every Saturday from 1 August to 26 December 2026, 08:00-12:00, which is shorter than the 07:00-13:00 our old record gave. Come early for the producers. On auction weekend the halles are the sale room, and no source says whether Saturday 14 November runs as normal, so check with the tourist office before sending guests.", "signature": "A wedge of Époisses and a slice of jambon persillé, bought from the producers before 10:00", "caveat": "08:00-12:00 per the tourist office; Saturday 14 Nov (auction weekend) not confirmed; cash useful at small stalls", "dishes": [{"name": "Époisses", "note": "The washed-rind cheese of the Côte d'Or, from the cheese stalls", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Cîteaux", "note": "The abbey cheese made by the monks north of Beaune", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Jambon persillé", "note": "Ham set in parsley jelly, sold by the slice by the charcutiers", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Autumn mushrooms", "note": "Girolles and other wild mushrooms in season", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Local honey", "note": "From the hill-village producers", "kind": "sweet"}], "neighborhood": "Place de la Halle", "signal_chip": {"label": "Sat 8-12", "full": "Every Saturday 08:00-12:00, Place de la Halle and Place Fleury, listed 1 August to 26 December 2026", "cosign": "Office de Tourisme de Beaune; JDS; Unidivers"}, "category": "street", "hot_this_month": "Époisses, Cîteaux, jambon persillé and the autumn mushrooms, 08:00 to 12:00 by the tourist office; whether Saturday 14 November, the auction weekend, trades as usual is not confirmed."},
    {"id": "v-charcuterie-raillard", "cat": "shop", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 1, "name": "Charcuterie Raillard", "short": "Charcuterie Raillard", "lat": null, "lng": null, "tags": [], "productTags": ["Charcuterie"], "address": "4 Rue Monge, 21200 Beaune", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Charcuterie+Raillard+4+rue+Monge+Beaune", "why": "Eddy Raillard, a charcutier from Le Creusot who trained at Bize in Savigny-lès-Beaune, fills his counter on rue Monge with the Burgundian repertoire: jambon persillé set in its green parsley jelly, pâté en croûte, terrine de campagne, boudin blanc, rosette and dry saucisson, and snails in parsley butter. A queue forms on busy mornings. Buy a thick slice and bread nearby and lunch is done standing up.", "verdict": "The shop exists at 4 rue Monge in public listings and a 2025 review, and Pudlowski called the jambon persillé a model of the genre in 2018, but nothing dated 2026 turned up and the hours on record are from 2018. Reviews praise the pâté en croûte and the persillé and grumble about the welcome. Call before you plan a lunch on it.", "signature": "A thick slice of jambon persillé, with bread and a cornichon", "caveat": "Closed Sunday and Monday morning in 2018; two phone numbers in circulation; reviews mention a brusque welcome and a queue", "person": "", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-25", "hook": "Eddy Raillard's charcuterie at 4 rue Monge: jambon persillé, pâté en croûte and boudin blanc over the counter.", "dishes": [{"name": "Jambon persillé", "note": "The house benchmark: Pudlowski (2018) called it a model of the genre", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Pâté en croûte", "note": "The item reviewers praise most", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Boudin blanc", "note": "Named in the 2018 Pudlowski piece", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Escargots persillés", "note": "Snails in parsley butter to take away", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Rosette and saucisson sec", "note": "The dry sausages, for a picnic between cellars", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Terrine de campagne", "note": "Country terrine, part of the core range", "kind": "dish"}], "hours": "Year-round as far as found. Open now (late Oct): probably, unconfirmed. Nov-Dec: no closure published. Auction weekend: Fri 13 and Sat 14 Nov fall on its days (2018 hours); Sun 15 Nov closed if the 2018 Sunday closure still holds · Call ahead: Pudlowski (2018) gives 10:00-13:00 and 15:00-19:00, closed Monday morning and Sunday; a directory says open until 19:00; no 2026 hours found", "phone": "Call ahead: +33 3 80 22 23 04 (acceslibre, directories) or +33 3 80 30 38 88 (Pudlowski 2018)", "reservation": "Walk-in shop", "neighborhood": "Place Monge", "signal_chip": {"label": "Pudlo 2018", "full": "Gilles Pudlowski, 2018: Eddy Raillard's jambon persillé, a model of the genre", "cosign": "acceslibre (address); Yelp listing updated Dec 2024; a 2025 review"}, "badge": "CHARCUTIER", "category": "street", "hot_this_month": "A thick slice of jambon persillé from rue Monge for a cold-morning picnic between cellars; call for the hours, the only ones found are from 2018."},
    {"id": "v16-p-tisserie-fabien-berteau", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 16, "badge": "PÂTISSERIE", "name": "Pâtisserie Fabien Berteau", "short": "Pâtisserie Fabien Bertea", "lat": 47.0228, "lng": 4.8376, "tags": [], "productTags": ["Cafe", "Bread"], "why": "Fabien Berteau was Gault&Millau's pastry chef of the year in 2015, working beside Jean-François Rouquette at the Park Hyatt Paris-Vendôme, where his cheesecakes were the signature. He then opened his own shop on rue Monge, a short walk from the Hospices. The counter runs from entremets and red-fruit tarts to bonbons de chocolat, and the cheesecake came with him; a small salon de thé lets you eat the cake on the spot.", "address": "18 Rue Monge, 21200 Beaune", "phone": "", "hours": "Year-round as far as found; no annual closure published. Open now (late Oct): yes on its days if the Feb 2026 hours hold. Nov-Dec: no closure published; Christmas hours unknown. Auction weekend: open Fri 13, Sat 14, Sun 15 (morning) and Mon 16 Nov on the listed hours · Mon, Tue, Thu, Fri 09:30-19:00; Sat 09:00-19:00; Sun 09:00-13:00; closed Wednesday (Cylex, updated 4 Feb 2026; myboulange and Justacoté agree on the Wednesday closure)", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pâtisserie+Fabien+Berteau+Beaune", "price_range": "EUR 3-9 (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-25", "hook": "A former Park Hyatt pastry chef's shop on rue Monge: cheesecake, Saint-Honoré, chocolates, a small tea room.", "verdict": "Gault&Millau keeps him in its artisan listing and directory pages were updated in February 2026, but no review or post dated 2026 surfaced, so trading is likely rather than proven. The pastry is the reason to go; several reviewers find the service cool. The Sunday-morning opening makes it one of the few good stops on auction Sunday.", "signature": "The cheesecake, the dish he brought from the Park Hyatt", "caveat": "Closed Wednesday; Sunday mornings only; reviews mention cool, slow service", "person": "Fabien Berteau (pastry chef)", "dishes": [{"name": "Cheesecake", "note": "His signature since the Park Hyatt years, cited by Gault&Millau", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Saint-Honoré", "note": "The classic reviewers name most", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Millefeuille", "note": "Another reviewer favourite", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Tarte au citron meringuée", "note": "Lemon meringue tart from the counter", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Macarons", "note": "Small and portable, for the boat", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Bonbons de chocolat", "note": "Filled chocolates, named by Gault&Millau", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Flan", "note": "Praised in a customer review", "kind": "sweet"}], "neighborhood": "Rue Monge", "signal_chip": {"label": "G&M 2015", "full": "Gault&Millau Pâtissier de l'année 2015 (then at the Park Hyatt Paris-Vendôme); listed in the Gault&Millau artisan guide at 18 rue Monge", "cosign": "Journal des Palaces (2015); Gault&Millau"}, "category": "street"}
